1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,581
The GraphQL module exposes your content to API clients.

2
00:00:04,581 --> 00:00:09,688
This video covers the options that limit queries, the permissions that decide who

3
00:00:09,688 --> 00:00:14,150
can run them, and how to hide types, parts and fields from the schema.

4
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:24,329
The options live in the OrchardCore section of the configuration, under Apis, GraphQL.

5
00:00:24,329 --> 00:00:28,270
This is shell configuration, so a tenant can override them.

6
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:30,150
Every option is optional.

7
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:36,597
DefaultNumberOfResults is the number of results a content type query returns when it

8
00:00:36,597 --> 00:00:39,445
sets no first argument, 100 by default.

9
00:00:39,445 --> 00:00:45,142
MaxNumberOfResults is the maximum for the first and last arguments, 1000 by default.

10
00:00:45,142 --> 00:00:48,370
A separate video covers the paging arguments.

11
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:53,985
MaxNumberOfResultsValidationMode decides what happens above that maximum.

12
00:00:53,985 --> 00:00:58,789
Enabled raises a validation error, and Disabled logs the excess instead.

13
00:00:58,789 --> 00:01:03,900
Default means Enabled in the Development environment, and Disabled otherwise.

14
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:08,791
MaxDepth limits how deeply a query can nest, 100 by default.

15
00:01:08,791 --> 00:01:14,500
MaxComplexity limits the complexity of a query, and FieldImpact sets what each object

16
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:15,942
field adds to it.

17
00:01:15,942 --> 00:01:17,950
Neither is set by default.

18
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:23,770
ExposeExceptions sends exception details, such as stack traces, to clients.

19
00:01:23,770 --> 00:01:27,650
It is on by default only in the Development environment.

20
00:01:31,850 --> 00:01:38,570
Every request to the endpoint, and the Tools, GraphiQL menu item, needs the Execute GraphQL permission.

21
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:41,529
Anonymous users do not have it by default.

22
00:01:41,529 --> 00:01:46,030
Without it, the endpoint challenges the request for authentication.

23
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:50,715
A mutation operation needs Execute GraphQL Mutations.

24
00:01:50,715 --> 00:01:56,184
Execute GraphQL names that permission as one that implies it, so holding the

25
00:01:56,184 --> 00:02:00,052
mutations permission also satisfies Execute GraphQL.

26
00:02:00,052 --> 00:02:03,320
The Administrator role holds it by default.

27
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:05,943
Content has its own checks.

28
00:02:05,943 --> 00:02:09,859
A query on a content type needs View own content for that type.

29
00:02:09,859 --> 00:02:14,059
Users with View all content then get every item, and users with only

30
00:02:14,059 --> 00:02:16,670
View own content get the items they own.

31
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:22,439
The contentItem query, which takes a content item id, returns nothing when the

32
00:02:22,439 --> 00:02:24,410
user cannot view that item.

33
00:02:24,410 --> 00:02:29,250
Every item of a type query is also checked once more before it is returned.

34
00:02:30,894 --> 00:02:37,293
To let visitors run queries, edit the Anonymous role under Access Control, Roles.

35
00:02:37,293 --> 00:02:40,308
Search the permissions for GraphQL.

36
00:02:40,308 --> 00:02:45,604
Execute GraphQL and Execute GraphQL Mutations are listed together.

37
00:02:46,072 --> 00:02:50,582
Let's allow Execute GraphQL in the Allow column, and save the role.

38
00:02:51,044 --> 00:02:52,308
The role is saved.

39
00:02:52,308 --> 00:02:56,942
Anonymous requests can reach the endpoint, and the content permissions of the role

40
00:02:56,942 --> 00:02:58,364
decide what they see.

41
00:02:59,964 --> 00:03:03,125
In your own types, RequirePermission protects a field.

42
00:03:03,125 --> 00:03:07,339
The permission is checked while the query is validated, and a user without

43
00:03:07,339 --> 00:03:10,342
it gets an authorization error with the status 401.

44
00:03:10,342 --> 00:03:14,504
The second argument is an optional resource, such as a content type name.

45
00:03:18,754 --> 00:03:23,025
GraphiQL is the query editor of the module, and its Explorer lists a

46
00:03:23,025 --> 00:03:27,181
query for each content type without a stereotype, such as article.

47
00:03:27,181 --> 00:03:32,144
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, and edit the Article type.

48
00:03:32,605 --> 00:03:36,189
On the type, Hide removes it from the GraphQL schema.

49
00:03:36,189 --> 00:03:38,195
Let's select Hide and save.

50
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:42,410
The schema is rebuilt when a content definition changes.

51
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:46,040
Back in GraphiQL, the Explorer no longer lists article.

52
00:03:47,675 --> 00:03:50,183
Each part of a type has options too.

53
00:03:50,183 --> 00:03:55,436
Let's open Design, Content Definition, Content Types, edit the Blog Post type, and

54
00:03:55,436 --> 00:03:57,465
edit its Markdown body part.

55
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:01,998
Collapse adds the fields of a part directly to the content type, and

56
00:04:01,998 --> 00:04:05,084
selecting it reveals Prevent Field Name Collision.

57
00:04:05,084 --> 00:04:07,950
Hide removes the part from the GraphQL schema.

58
00:04:08,410 --> 00:04:12,648
On the Autoroute part, Collapse is selected and disabled, with a note that

59
00:04:12,648 --> 00:04:14,396
it is collapsed by default.

60
00:04:14,396 --> 00:04:17,310
The Autoroute module collapses that part in code.

61
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:26,194
Options in code go through the GraphQL content options, in a Startup class.

62
00:04:26,194 --> 00:04:31,399
IgnoreField removes a field from the content item types and from their where filter.

63
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:33,250
Here it removes the owner.

64
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:40,226
ConfigurePart collapses or hides a part for every content type, as the Autoroute module does.

65
00:04:40,226 --> 00:04:45,950
ConfigureContentType hides a content type, or a query of a module such as SiteLayers.

66
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:53,370
A content type with a stereotype gets a query only when DiscoverableSterotypes lists that stereotype.

67
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:56,947
Options in code can only turn a setting on.

68
00:04:56,947 --> 00:05:02,140
Hidden set to false does not undo what an editor selected, so the type stays hidden.

69
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:08,976
Configuration options limit what queries can ask for, permissions decide who can ask,

70
00:05:08,976 --> 00:05:12,378
and hidden types and fields decide what the schema offers.

71
00:05:12,378 --> 00:05:13,760
Thanks for watching.

